      <p class="/_attributes/common-attributes.md"></p>
      <p>Jobs execute one-time or scheduled tasks in your cluster, tracking completion status and managing pod lifecycles for batch workloads, parallel processing, and recurring operations.</p>
      <p>A <em>job</em> executes a task in your OpenShift Container Platform cluster.</p>
      <p>A job tracks the overall progress of a task and updates its status with information about active, succeeded, and failed pods. Deleting a job cleans up any pod replicas it created. Jobs are part of the Kubernetes API, which can be managed with <code>oc</code> commands like other object types.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: Job\nmetadata:\n  name: pi\nspec:\n  parallelism: 1\n  completions: 1\n  activeDeadlineSeconds: 1800\n  backoffLimit: 6\n  ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 100\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      name: pi\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: pi\n        image: perl\n        command: [\"perl\",  \"-Mbignum=bpi\", \"-wle\", \"print bpi(2000)\"]\n      restartPolicy: OnFailure\n#..."} lang="yaml" title="Sample Job specification" />
